# Storage Services

11. S3 (Simple Storage Service)
Amazon S3 is an object storage service used to store files such as images, videos, documents, backups, and application data. It is highly durable, scalable, and accessible from anywhere over the internet.

12. EBS (Elastic Block Store)
Amazon EBS provides block-level storage volumes that can be attached to EC2 instances. It is mainly used as the primary storage for operating systems, applications, and databases running on EC2.

13. EFS (Elastic File System)
Amazon EFS is a fully managed file storage service that allows multiple EC2 instances to access the same shared file system simultaneously. It is commonly used for shared applications and content management systems.

14. Glacier
Amazon Glacier is a low-cost cloud storage service designed for long-term backup and data archiving. It is ideal for storing data that is rarely accessed but must be retained for months or years.

