# Load Balancing & Scaling
32. Elastic Load Balancer (ELB)
Definition:
Elastic Load Balancer automatically distributes incoming traffic across multiple servers or EC2 instances. It improves application availability, reliability, and performance by preventing any single server from becoming overloaded.

33. Auto Scaling Group (ASG)

Definition:
An Auto Scaling Group automatically increases or decreases the number of EC2 instances based on application demand. It helps maintain performance while reducing infrastructure costs.

34. Scaling Concepts

Definition:
Scaling is the process of increasing or decreasing computing resources to handle changing workloads. It ensures applications remain available during high traffic while optimizing resource usage.

Types:

Vertical Scaling (Increase server capacity)
Horizontal Scaling (Add more servers)
35. Global Deployment

Definition:
Global Deployment is the process of deploying an application across multiple AWS regions or availability zones. It reduces latency, improves fault tolerance, and ensures high availability for users worldwide.


